1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stina_Piper '''Christina "''Stina''" Charlotta Piper'''] was a Swedish freight manager and countess.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''She was the''' daughter of Carl Fredrik Piper and Ulrika Christina Mörner af Morlanda. She was the granddaughter of Christina Piper. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1754 she married''' [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erik_Brahe '''Erik Brahe'''], who was executed in 1756 for participating in the queen's failed Coup of 1756. Piper, who was pregnant at the time of her husband's execution, 
2 CONC tried several times to get a more lenient sentence for her husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Piper had two''' children with Brahe: Ulrika Juliana and Magnus Fredrik Brahe. As a widow, Piper successfully managed the estates belonging to her son and step-sons' inheritance during their minority. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''During her years''' as a widow, she had a relationship with her cousin [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Ribbing_af_Koberg_nr_216 '''Carl Ribbing af Koberg'''] (1718-1773) , with whom she had three children between 1762 and
2 CONC  1769 who where raised in foster homes.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1773, she''' married riksråd [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Scheffer_nr_144 '''Ulrik Scheffer'''], a political opponent to Erik Brahe. As the wife of riksråd Scheffer, Piper was given the title ''riksrådinna'' and as 
2 CONC such had a role in the Swedish royal court's etiquette and ceremonial activities.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1783, the''' couple retired back to the Stora Ek estate. Scheffer died in 1799, after which Piper returned to Stockholm where she died a year later.
