1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pontus_De_la_Gardie '''Pontus De la Gardie'''] was a French nobleman and military in the service of Denmark and Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was born''' as '''Ponce d'Escouperie''' in Russol (Aude), Languedoc, as a son of Jacques Jacques Scorperier and Catherine de Sainte-Colombe. As a youngster, he wanted to become a priest and was educated in a monastery. He ch
2 CONC anged his mind however, and left Languedoc to become a mercenary in the service of Denmark. De la Gardie was promoted to officer and was in charge of a regiment of mercenaries. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1565, during''' the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northern_Seven_Years%27_War Northern Seven Years' War], he was captured by Swedish troops at Varberg, and changed allegiance to Sweden. De la Gardie quickly became a favouri
2 CONC te of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_III_of_Sweden John III of Sweden] and in 1569, after only four years in the Swedish service, he received noble status. In 1571, he was created a baron and was given [https://en.wikipedia.o
2 CONC rg/wiki/Ekholmen_Castle Ekholmen Castle].
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was then''' suspected to have taken part in a plot to assassinate John III. The plot was led by [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_de_Mornay Charles de Mornay], who was in contact with [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chri
2 CONC stina_of_Denmark Christina of Denmark] and the French ambassador in Copenhagen [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_Dan%C3%A7ay Charles Dançay]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John III was''' to be killed during a swords dance performed by Scottish mercenaries at the party which was to be given in October that year before the Scottish mercenaries departure to the Baltic. After the assassination, the 
2 CONC king's brother [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_XI_of_Sweden Duke Charles] was to be placed upon the throne. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The plot did''' not materialize as de Mornay lost his nerve and never gave the sign to the mercenaries to take action. In September 1574, the plot was revealed and Charles de Mornay was arrested, interrogated and executed. It w
2 CONC as never made clear who participated in the plot. However, it is noted, that the suspected conspirators [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hogenskild_Bielke Hogenskild Bielke], [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gustaf_Ban%C3%A9r Gustaf B
2 CONC anér] and Pontus De la Gardie, often gathered at meetings in the apartment of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princess_Elizabeth_of_Sweden Princess Elizabeth of Sweden], meetings where  [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princess_Cecil
2 CONC ia_of_Sweden Princess Cecilia of Sweden] had also frequently been seen, and the two sisters and their brother Charles were somewhat compromised though they were never accused. Pontus De la Gardie was himself never put on trial for
2 CONC  his suspected involvement in the affair.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''After''' [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clas_%C3%85kesson_Tott Clas Åkesson Tott]'s resignation as the supreme commander of the Swedish forces in Finland and Estonia as a consequence of the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siege_
2 CONC of_Wesenberg_(1574 Siege of Wesenberg] (1574) during the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Livonian_War Livonian War], De la Gardie took over Tott's office. De la Gardie's skills combined with the fact that Sweden's enemy Russia had 
2 CONC to transfer troops to defend against Polish attacks further south led to considerable military success for Sweden during the following years. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In the fall''' of 1580, Karelia was conquered. De la Gardie led his troops over the frozen Gulf of Finland to capture the fortresses of Wesenberg (now Rakvere) and Tolsburg (now Toolse). In September 1581, Narva was taken after
2 CONC  a storming that had been preceded by a massive bombardment. 4,000 soldiers and civilians were killed, pointing out the fact that De la Gardie was not only a skillful warrior, but a cruel and hard commander as well. De la Gardie a
2 CONC nd his Swedish / Finnish troops went on to capture the fortress of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivangorod Ivangorod] and several other fortresses that autumn. In 1582, the war with Russia was ended and Sweden got to keep the con
2 CONC quests made in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karelia Karelia] and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ingria Ingria], but had to withdraw from Livonia.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''De la Gardie''' was the most renowned military commander in Sweden during the 16th century and has been credited with much of the country's military success in the 1580s. An example of his ingenuity was the strategy of using zi
2 CONC gzag shaped saps during the siege of Narva, a new technique at the time.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''De la Gardie''' drowned in the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narva_River Narva River] and is buried in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Mary%27s_Cathedral,_Tallinn St Mary's Cathedral] of Tallinn. His tomb chest is made by w
2 CONC ell-known artist and architect [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arent_Passer Arent Passer].
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Family''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 4 February''' 1580 De la Gardie married [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sofia_Gyllenhielm Sofia Johansdotter Gyllenhielm], the illegitimate daughter of John III of Sweden and the Finnish society lady [https://en.wikipedia.org
2 CONC /wiki/Karin_Hansdotter Karin Hansdotter]. During the wedding act, a gallery in the church broke and one person was killed. Some sceptics claimed it was a bad omen or a divine act with which God condemned the marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Pontus De la Gardie''' and Sofia Gyllenhielm had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Brita De la Gardie''' (Pontusdotter) (1581–1645),
2 CONT # '''Baron Johan De la Gardie''' (1582–1642), a statesman of the Swedish Empire, and 
2 CONT # '''Count and Field Marshal Jacob De la Gardie''' (1583–1652), a very significant military leader
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Further reading''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Arrhenius-Örnhiälm, Claudius (1625-1695) (1690). Vita Illustrissimi Herois Ponti De La Gardie, Excercituum Sveciae Supremi Campi Ducis, Regnante Johanne III. Svecorum Rege Gloriosissimo : Cujus occasione totius fere Livoniae His
2 CONC toria exhibetur ; Ex incorruptae veritatis monumentis ... concinnata. Lipsiae, Leipzig: Apud. Jo. Frider. Gleditsch. 
2 CONT
