1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Robert Lauder of the Bass
2 CONT *M, b. circa 1490, d. June 1576
2 CONT * Parents: Robert Lauder of the Bass and Edrington, and Elizabeth Lawson.1 
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Lauder of the Bass was born circa 1490.1 He died in June 1576.1
2 CONT
2 CONT # He married, firstly, Margaret Sinclair, daughter of Sir Oliver Sinclair of Roslin and Margaret Borthwick.2 
2 CONT # He married, secondly,  Elizabeth Hay, daughter of John Hay, 4th Lord Hay of Yester, by an unknown mistress
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family notes 
2 CONT His second wife was *Elizabeth*, illegitimate daughter of John 4th Lord Hay of Yester (some references say 3rd Lord but this is incorrect - he would be too old plus he had a legitimate daughter named Elizabeth). In Elizabeth's Let
2 CONC ters of Legitimation she is described as the "bastard daughter of John Hay, Lord of Yester." She is mentioned in numerous records always as Elizabeth and wife (and relict) of Robert Lauder of The Bass.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Hay married the eldest son and heir-apparent of this Robert Lauder of The Bass, another Sir Robert Lauder, of Poppil. He died v.p.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Extracted from https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Lauder-91
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # http://www.thepeerage.com/p60648.htm#i606480 “He married, secondly, Alison Cranstoun.”
