1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JAMES HERIOT OF TRABROUN===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Heriot of Trabroun is the son of James Heriot of Trabroun. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi05scot#page/382/mode/1up RMS: 1151]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Heriot of Trabroun died on 4 June 1618. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, Testament Dative of James Heriot of Trabroun, parish of Haddington, reference CC8/8/50]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===His Last Will and Testament===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Heriot of Trabroun made his last will and testament at Aldingstone in East Lothian on 22 October 1612. He nominated and appointed his wife Isabel Maitland to be his only executor and universal intromitter, to whom he left
2 CONC  his share of the free gear. The inventory of his moveable estate was given up by his widow, Isabel Maitland.  At the time of his death her deceased husband owed two hundred and sixty-six pounds thirteen shilling a four pence to h
2 CONC is son, Robert Heriot, younger of Trabroun (who is once referred to in error as Walter). Confirmation was granted to her on 3 April 1619. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, Testament Dative of James Heriot 
2 CONC of Trabroun, parish of Haddington, reference CC8/8/50]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000127090178082& Image of Testament]
