2 CONC skin feuar thereof for same reddendo; Ovir Howdane of the commendator and convent of Calco, rendering therefor £15 feu duty, Three suits at three head courts at the place of Calco yearly, and double feu duty at each heir's entry; 
2 CONC and Quhytlaw of ..... Lawder of Burnegranes for 2 pennies blench; and that all the above had been in non-entry for 23 days by reason of the death of James Heriot elder, who died 4 Oct instant. Names of the jury:- Alexander Dalmaho
2 CONC y of that ilk, Thomas Fawsyde of that ilk, Patrick Congiltoun of that ilk, David Rentoun younger of Byllie, Archibald Lorimer in Thirrilstane, George Cranstoun in Cauldscheill, Thomas Cranstoun, burgess of Lawder, William Lowthian
2 CONC e in Lylestoun, Henry Fairbarne in Gordoun, Niniane Fairbarne indweller there, Richard Edgar in Cummerlawis, Thoams Greif in Thirrilstane, Patrick Newtoun younger of that ilk, Christopher Knowis, portioner of that ilk, Henry Ogill
2 CONC  of Hartramewode. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH6%2f2571&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+heriot+of+trabroun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Register House 
2 CONC charters, 1st series, reference RH6/2571]'''
