1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===RICHARD HERIOT OF TRABROUN younger (aka RIC. HERIOT apparenti de Trabroun)===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death has not been identified for Robert Heriot of Trabroun, younger. He was alive on 16 March 1593, [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi06scot/page/30 RMS: 81] but he must have died before 29 Janua
2 CONC ry 1603, when his younger brother Robert is identified as their father's son and heir. . [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi07scot#page/210/mode/1up RMS: 563]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 March 1593: Charter by James, Earl of Arran, made in favour of John, Lord Thirlestane. Witness by Richard Heriot, apparent of Trabroun. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi06scot/page/30 Registrum Magni Sigilli Regu
2 CONC m Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1593-1608, charter number 81 on pp. 30-1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 29 and 31 January 1603 James Heriot of Trabroun and his son and heir Robert Heriot were cautioners for Lady Jean Fleming, Countess of Cassillis: "Jac Hereot de Trabroun et Rob. H. ejus filium et heredem apparentem". [https:/
2 CONC /archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi07scot#page/210/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorm. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A. D. 1609-1620, charter number 563 on page 210]'''
